vulkan_occlusion_queries_in_render_pass (off, hot reload; to measure with 0127's counters before turning it on): 0053
ends the render pass around every occlusion query begin and end. Samples only come from draws, which only happen in
render passes, so in this mode the host query runs inside each guest render pass the guest query spans: a segment
begun right after the pass begins (or at the guest's begin, inside a pass) and ended before it ends (or at the
guest's end), the guest result being the sum of its segments. Render target cache transfer passes are not the
guest's draws and get no segment. Query indices are reset ahead in blocks of 64 outside render passes (a reset is
not allowed inside one), and the results are copied to the readback buffer at the end of the submission (neither is
a copy). Wrapping the indices around waits for results in flight, so it is only done where the guest begins a query;
a pass entered without an index left gets no segment. With the mode off nothing changes.

